@wuxibin89 On the vLLM patches this PR still carries (vLLM 0.32):
1. **Per-token compressed-tensors MoE** (`install_nvfp4_per_token_compressed_tensors_patch`): vLLM supports per-token NVFP4 activations for ModelOpt (vllm-project/vllm#56740) but not for compressed-tensors. Upstream PR: vllm-project/vllm#64209. Once it lands, verl only passes the activation override, and the subclass goes away.
2. **`clear_kv_cache` at start-up**: with dummy weights the scales are zero, so per-token quantization of the all-zero MoE rows writes NaN into the KV cache. vLLM main has since changed dummy initialization; we will drop this after the next vLLM upgrade, once verified.
